# BananaOS Architecture Rule

## Monorepo Layout

```
apps/api/src/          # Express API
  database/models/     # Mongoose schemas
  services/            # Business logic
  api/controllers/     # Request handlers (Zod + asyncHandler)
  api/routes/          # Route mounting

apps/web/src/
  apps/<app>/          # One folder per BananaOS app
  services/            # Shared APIs (simApi, contactsApi, appRouter)
  stores/              # Global Zustand (auth, OS, windows)
  components/os/       # Shell (HomeScreen, Dock, LockScreen)

packages/shared/       # Shared types (SocketEvent, etc.)
```

## App Module Pattern

Each app: `manifest.ts` · `index.tsx` · `types.ts` · `store/` · `services/` · `screens/` · `hooks/use*Realtime.ts` · `__tests__/`

## Backend Pattern

```typescript
// Controller
function auditCtx(req: AuthRequest, permission: PermName): AuditContext { ... }
await checkPerm(req, 'view_resource');
const data = schema.parse(req.body);
res.json({ success: true, data: formatEntity(entity) });

// Service owns business logic, audit logs, socket emits
```

## Frontend Data

- Server state: TanStack Query (`queryKey: ['app', 'resource']`)
- UI state: Zustand store per app
- Realtime: `use*Realtime()` invalidates query keys on socket events

## API Responses

Always `{ success: boolean, data?: T, error?: string }`. Use `apiRequest` from `@/utils/api`.

## Database Models

Include `timestamps: true`. Add `createdBy`/`updatedBy`/`deletedAt` when the entity is user-managed. Index foreign keys and search fields.

## Don't

- Put business logic in controllers
- Create parallel routing systems outside `appRouter.ts`
- Skip route registration in `apps/api/src/index.ts`
